      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T18:16:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The code has the following, though:\n\n```\n            long secureUserId \u003d GateKeeper.getSecureUserId(userId);\n            if (secureUserId \u003d\u003d GateKeeper.INVALID_SECURE_USER_ID) {\n                return BIOMETRIC_NO_AUTHENTICATION;\n            }\n```\n\nUsers have a SID if and only if they have a secure lock screen.  So, if the user\u0027s lock screen is changed to swipe or none, then the API actually starts returning `BIOMETRIC_NO_AUTHENTICATION`.  Is that WAI and clearly documented?",
      "parentUuid": "5fda3b43_3aef0a08",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "246d57f63f400b99fae8f9bfaf0a2aee59c29cdc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62c580b8_45f2ec0b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/hardware/biometrics/BiometricManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 660,
      "author": {
        "id": 1974730
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T21:59:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ugh, good catch. For the expected usage this isn\u0027t a concern, but I would prefer this API to continue returning values here. Unfortunately, I think it\u0027s probably too much work to fix this edge case right now.\n\nWe could document that if the user removes their secure lock screen that this will always return NO_AUTHENTICATION, even if successful authentications have occurred prior to the removal (and after boot). If we later fix this, we can amend the doc to say that it will return those times after SDK 45 or whatever. Does that sound reasonable?",
      "parentUuid": "d9c43e1b_8b0b9532",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "246d57f63f400b99fae8f9bfaf0a2aee59c29cdc",
